---
name: bp3g-no-human
description: Run several bp3 graphs with no human present using the bp3g conductor — fleet preflight, park blocked work in the inbox, and end with the check-in report; never attests, never pages, never promotes.
---

# Bp3g, no human

Use when a human in a bp3-enabled repo invokes this skill
by name (`/bp3g-no-human <graph>...`,
`$bp3g-no-human`) or asks to run graphs unattended,
overnight, or in a queue with no human present. Several
graphs may be named; a Run budget may be stated. One
output: the check-in report (step 5). For one graph with a
human present, use `bp3g` instead.

`/bp3g-no-human <graph>...` means `/bp3g <graph>` per
graph, in queue order, under the no-human rails below. Follow
the canonical `bp3g` skill (`skills/bp3g/SKILL.md`)
procedure and rules as written there — read state with
`bp3 g r`, dispatch the one step that state calls for,
re-read. This file carries no step procedure of its own,
so the two names cannot drift; it adds only the rails
that make the conductor safe with no human in the room.

## Shape

This ships as a skill mode of `bp3g`, not its own FSM.
The rails below (preflight, parking, budget, check-in report)
all state as conductor rules over the existing node FSM
without special cases: the queue is ordered iteration,

==> skills/bp3g-landing-demo/SKILL.md <==
---
name: bp3g-landing-demo
description: Produce the Landing IIUC for a bp3 Graph being promoted — diligence gate first (every node checked against its own acceptance; unsettled or improperly-done nodes route to red-ink, not landing), then decision record, settled picture, demo traces, files touched, verification, and deliberately-open items.
---

# Red-Ink Graph Landing Demo

Use when a human or Controller in bp3 invokes this skill by
name (`/red-ink-bp3g-landing-demo`), when a Graph reaches
Graph-to-master promotion, or when asked “walk me through
what this graph became / what got done / give me the demos.”
One output: a Landing IIUC, presented in chat and, on human
approval, recorded at the Graph's landing.

Use `graph` instead to frame a new Graph. Use `using-bp3`
to operate graph state. Use `icebox` to freeze a deferred
idea. Use `red-ink` while a design is still being decided.

## The diligence gate (runs first, always)

Landing is a claim: every node did what its `EXPERIMENT.md`
promised. Before any playback, check each node:

| Check | Pass evidence |
|---|---|
| Design settled | no open questions in the node; no unadopted `EXPERIMENT.red-ink.md` working copy |
| Acceptance met | every Acceptance case has `observed` evidence (run output, ledger line, test), not prose |
| Review judged the node, not just the code | the review verdict binds the bound commit AND the node's acceptance cases |

Any node failing a check stops the landing. Do not present
