|---|---|---|
| graph | graph | the whole work graph; a goal pursued as a graph. CLI door: `bp3 g` (graph create/read/update/delete) |
| node door | (new) | CLI door per noun: `bp3 n` (node read + edge calls). `bp3 g` = graph, `bp3 n` = node, `bp3 harness` = supervisor machinery — one door per noun (owner, red-ink round 1) |
| goal (G) | graph, as owner-facing word | G stands for goal and graph; skills are the `bp3g` family (`/bp3g`) because bare "goal" collides across harnesses |
| node | exp / experiment | one work unit in the graph; root worker dispatches nodes |
